NSTT Mesh Network Layer — rune‑encoded service fabric
Here’s the mesh layer that lets your agents discover, announce, and route to each other across machines, using rune‑encoded beacons and your existing transport/protocol.

1. Mesh roles
Mesh Orchestrator: global coordinator (already built NSTTOrchestrator)

Mesh Nodes: machines/containers running one or more agents

Mesh Registry: in‑memory or external (Redis/DB/etc.) index of active agents

2. Rune‑encoded service beacon
